Identify IDE/ATA Device                                                                 BTS6120.PLX


6757    11076    6477		PWCR			; ...
6758    11077    2051		ISZ	XFRCNT		; have we done all 256 bytes?
6759    11100    5265		 JMP	 IDDEV1		; nope - keep reading
6760                 	
6761                 	;   We've read our 256 bytes, but the drive still has another 256 more waiting
6762                 	; in the buffer.  We need to read those and throw them away...
6763    11101    1362		TAD	[-128.]		; we still need to read 128 more words
6764    11102    3051		DCA	XFRCNT		; ...
6765    11103    1360	IDDEV2:	TAD	[SETDRD]	; assert DIOR
6766    11104    6477		PWCR			; ...
6767    11105    7000		NOP			; make sure the DIOR pulse is wide enough
6768    11106    7000		NOP			; ...
6769    11107    1356		TAD	[CLRDRD]	; and then clear DIOR
6770    11110    6477		PWCR			; ...
