        11274    5764
6898                 	
6899                 	;   There's a subtle difference in the order of operations between reading and
6900                 	; writing.  In the case of writing, we send the WRITE SECTOR command to the
6901                 	; drive, transfer our data to the sector buffer, and only then does the
6902                 	; drive actually go out and access the disk.  This means we have to wait
6903                 	; one more time for the drive to actually finish writing, because only then
6904                 	; can we know whether it actually worked or not!
6905    11275    5772		JMP	@[WREADY]	; wait for the drive to finish writing

PALX - IM6100/HM6120 Assembly Language V3.32 RLA                      13-JAN-24  18:41:12   Page 170
